      <Link href={pageHref("/upstream/")}>Every bug we filed</Link>
    </p>
    <Notes>
      <p><strong>On screen:</strong> how many known bugs GMT works around, and how we check them.</p>
      <p><strong>Say:</strong> "A workaround is GMT's code that steps around someone else's bug, with a test. Every week a check runs those tests again. When the fix ships upstream, the check tells us, and we delete that workaround."</p>
    </Notes>
  </Slide>

  <Slide id="lint" title="Lint that bans Date" minutes={0.5} place="greenwich">
    <LintRules />
    <Notes>
      <p><strong>On screen:</strong> GMT's lint rules.</p>
      <p><strong>Say:</strong> "Our lint rules are strict on purpose. Every rule is an error, not a warning. They ban the name <code>Date</code> itself, not only <code>new Date()</code>. They also ban every import of a library built on Date. Oxlint and ESLint get all seven rules. Biome gets every rule except the ban on the name Date."</p>
    </Notes>
